% Spinal Orthoses: TLSO and LSO — LCD L33790 and its Policy Article A52500
% (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills, the
% face-to-face and prior authorization lists) and states when a claim for a
% lumbar-sacral (LSO) or thoracic-lumbar-sacral (TLSO) orthosis (L0450–L0651,
% the 51 codes of the LCD) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
%   - the orthosis is ordered for one of the LCD's four indications: to
%     reduce pain by restricting mobility of the trunk; to facilitate healing
%     following an injury to the spine or related soft tissues; to
%     facilitate healing following a surgical procedure on the spine or
%     related soft tissue; to otherwise support weak spinal muscles and/or a
%     deformed spine;
%   - a custom fabricated orthosis (L0452, L0480, L0482, L0484, L0486, L0622,
%     L0624, L0629, L0632, L0634, L0636, L0638, L0640) is medically necessary
%     rather than a prefabricated one. The LCD states no criterion for custom
%     fabrication; the Policy Article requires the treating practitioner's
%     records to support "the medical necessity of the custom fabricated
%     orthosis rather than a prefabricated orthosis", and this program reads
%     that as a coverage criterion, as afo_kafo.le does.
% The protective body sock (L0984) does not meet the definition of a brace:
% the policy decides it but places it in no benefit. The benefit is not
% durable medical equipment: the Policy Article places LSOs and TLSOs under
% the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9)).
%
% How the criteria are read. The indication is what the record documents:
% the shared template "the medical record of B documents C", with the
% conditions the four indications name (pain requiring restricted trunk
% mobility, spinal injury, spinal soft tissue injury, spinal surgery, weak
% spinal muscles, spinal deformity) as facts of this program citing the LCD.
% One criterion is a judgment — the judged template of dmepos.le:
%   custom fabrication required (a custom fabricated orthosis: the need for
%   custom fabrication rather than a prefabricated orthosis, recorded by the
%   treating practitioner).
% The Policy Article's ICD-10 section names no code list (no table is
% loaded: sources/icd10 has none for A52500).
%
% The payment conditions the Policy Article adds ("Policy specific
% documentation requirements"), in section remedy: for a custom fabricated
% orthosis the orthotist's functional evaluation corroborating the need; for
% a custom fitted orthosis (L0454, L0456, L0458, L0460, L0462, L0464, L0466,
% L0468, L0470, L0472, L0488, L0490, L0491, L0492, L0626, L0627, L0630,
% L0631, L0633, L0635, L0637, L0639) the supplier's records describing why
% the modifications at the fitting were necessary and what they were. The
% face-to-face encounter and the written order before delivery (L0456,
% L0457, L0486, L0631, L0635–L0640, L0648, L0650, L0651) and the prior
% authorization (L0456, L0457, L0486, L0631, L0637, L0639, L0648, L0650,
% L0651) are dmepos.le's, read from the CMS lists.
%
% Not modelled: the OTS versus custom fitted coding (minimal
% self-adjustment at delivery) and the characteristics of each code (rigid
% posterior panel, body jacket, TLSO height: an item's code is taken as
% correct); the hospital and SNF payment rules (an orthosis provided within
% two days of discharge); the CG modifier; the PDAC coding verification;
% the elastic garments coded A4467 (a code several orthotic policies deny;
% none models it).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of afo_kafo.le and knee_orthoses.le)
    the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of *an item*; undefined.
    the records of the supplier justify the modifications made at the fitting of *an item*; undefined.
    % the codes and the lists
    *a condition* is an indication for a spinal orthosis.
    code *a code* is excluded from the braces benefit of spinal orthoses.
    % derived
    *an item* is a spinal orthosis.
    *an item* is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis.
    *an item* is a custom fitted spinal orthosis.
    *a beneficiary* has an indication for a spinal orthosis.
    the spinal custom fabrication criteria are met for *an item*.
    the spinal custom fabrication documentation is met for *an item*.
    the custom fitting documentation is met for *an item*.

the knowledge base spinal_orthoses includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base spinal_orthoses includes:

LCD L33790 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33790".
the text of LCD L33790 is at "sources/lcd/L33790.txt".
Policy Article A52500 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52500".
the text of Policy Article A52500 is at "sources/article/A52500.txt".

% What the items are, by code.
rule spinal_orthosis_device with provenance LCD L33790,
        confer "A spinal orthosis (L0450, L0452, L0454, L0455, L0456, L0457, L0458, L0460, L0462, L0464, L0466, L0467, L0468, L0469, L0470, L0472, L0480, L0482, L0484, L0486, L0488, L0490, L0491, L0492, L0621, L0622, L0623, L0624, L0625, L0626, L0627, L0628, L0629, L0630, L0631, L0632, L0633, L0634, L0635, L0636, L0637, L0638, L0639, L0640, L0641, L0642, L0643, L0648, L0649, L0650, L0651) is covered when it is ordered for one of the following indications":
an item is a spinal orthosis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L0450", "L0452", "L0454", "L0455", "L0456", "L0457", "L0458", "L0460", "L0462", "L0464", "L0466", "L0467", "L0468", "L0469", "L0470", "L0472", "L0480", "L0482", "L0484", "L0486", "L0488", "L0490", "L0491", "L0492", "L0621", "L0622", "L0623", "L0624", "L0625", "L0626", "L0627", "L0628", "L0629", "L0630", "L0631", "L0632", "L0633", "L0634", "L0635", "L0636", "L0637", "L0638", "L0639", "L0640", "L0641", "L0642", "L0643", "L0648", "L0649", "L0650", "L0651"].

rule spinal_custom_fabricated_device with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "For a custom fabricated orthosis (L0452, L0480, L0482, L0484, L0486, L0622, L0624, L0629, L0632, L0634, L0636, L0638 and L0640), there must be detailed documentation in the treating practitioner’s records":
an item is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L0452", "L0480", "L0482", "L0484", "L0486", "L0622", "L0624", "L0629", "L0632", "L0634", "L0636", "L0638", "L0640"].

rule spinal_custom_fitted_device with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "Items requiring more than minimal self-adjustment by a qualified practitioner are coded as custom fitted (L0454, L0456, L0458, L0460, L0462, L0464, L0466, L0468, L0470, L0472, L0488, L0490, L0491, L0492, L0626, L0627, L0630, L0631, L0633, L0635, L0637 and L0639)":
an item is a custom fitted spinal orthosis
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["L0454", "L0456", "L0458", "L0460", "L0462", "L0464", "L0466", "L0468", "L0470", "L0472", "L0488", "L0490", "L0491", "L0492", "L0626", "L0627", "L0630", "L0631", "L0633", "L0635", "L0637", "L0639"].

% The conditions of the record the four indications name.
pain requiring restricted trunk mobility is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To reduce pain by restricting mobility of the trunk".
spinal injury is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To facilitate healing following an injury to the spine or related soft tissues".
spinal soft tissue injury is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To facilitate healing following an injury to the spine or related soft tissues".
spinal surgery is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To facilitate healing following a surgical procedure on the spine or related soft tissue".
weak spinal muscles is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To otherwise support weak spinal muscles and/or a deformed spine".
spinal deformity is an indication for a spinal orthosis,
    as stated in LCD L33790, confer "To otherwise support weak spinal muscles and/or a deformed spine".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the LSOs and TLSOs of the LCD, and the
% protective body sock the Article denies.
rule spinal_codes with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "Lumbar-sacral orthoses (LSO) and thoracic-lumbar-sacral orthoses (TLSO) are covered under the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the policy for code a code is spinal_orthoses
    if the code is in ["L0450", "L0452", "L0454", "L0455", "L0456", "L0457", "L0458", "L0460", "L0462", "L0464", "L0466", "L0467", "L0468", "L0469", "L0470", "L0472", "L0480", "L0482", "L0484", "L0486", "L0488", "L0490", "L0491", "L0492", "L0621", "L0622", "L0623", "L0624", "L0625", "L0626", "L0627", "L0628", "L0629", "L0630", "L0631", "L0632", "L0633", "L0634", "L0635", "L0636", "L0637", "L0638", "L0639", "L0640", "L0641", "L0642", "L0643", "L0648", "L0649", "L0650", "L0651", "L0984"].

section applicability is:

% The benefit: not durable medical equipment but the braces benefit of
% Social Security Act §1861(s)(9) — for every code but the body sock.
rule spinal_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "Lumbar-sacral orthoses (LSO) and thoracic-lumbar-sacral orthoses (TLSO) are covered under the Medicare braces benefit (Social Security Act §1861(s)(9))":
the benefit category of code a code is braces
    if the policy for code the code is spinal_orthoses
    and it is not the case that
        code the code is excluded from the braces benefit of spinal orthoses.

code "L0984" is excluded from the braces benefit of spinal orthoses,
    as stated in Policy Article A52500, confer "A protective body sock (L0984) does not meet the definition of a brace and is noncovered".

section question is:

rule spinal_covered with provenance LCD L33790,
        confer "is covered when it is ordered for one of the following indications":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a spinal orthosis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary has an indication for a spinal orthosis
    and the spinal custom fabrication criteria are met for the item.

rule spinal_indication with provenance LCD L33790,
        confer "If a spinal orthosis is provided and the coverage criteria are not met, the item will be denied as not medically necessary":
a beneficiary has an indication for a spinal orthosis
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is an indication for a spinal orthosis.

% A custom fabricated orthosis: the treating practitioner's records support
% its medical necessity rather than a prefabricated one's (the finding).
rule spinal_custom_criteria with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "there must be detailed documentation in the treating practitioner’s records to support the medical necessity of the custom fabricated orthosis rather than a prefabricated orthosis":
the spinal custom fabrication criteria are met for an item
    if the item is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the finding custom fabrication required about the beneficiary is established.

% a prefabricated orthosis needs no reason for custom fabrication: a device of this model
rule spinal_prefabricated:
the spinal custom fabrication criteria are met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own conditions of payment (Policy Article A52500, "Policy
% specific documentation requirements").
rule spinal_documentation with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "Have detailed documentation in the supplier’s record that justifies the code selected":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is spinal_orthoses
    and the claim is for an item
    and the spinal custom fabrication documentation is met for the item
    and the custom fitting documentation is met for the item.

rule spinal_orthotist_records with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "This information will be corroborated by the functional evaluation in the orthotist’s records":
the spinal custom fabrication documentation is met for an item
    if the item is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis
    and the records of the orthotist include a functional evaluation corroborating the need for custom fabrication of the item.

% a prefabricated orthosis: a device of this model
rule spinal_no_custom_fabrication_documentation:
the spinal custom fabrication documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a custom fabricated spinal orthosis.

rule spinal_custom_fitting_records with provenance Policy Article A52500,
        confer "Documentation must be sufficiently detailed to include, but is not limited to, a detailed description of why the modifications are necessary and what modifications were performed at the time of fitting the orthosis to the beneficiary":
the custom fitting documentation is met for an item
    if the item is a custom fitted spinal orthosis
    and the records of the supplier justify the modifications made at the fitting of the item.

% an off-the-shelf or custom fabricated orthosis: a device of this model
rule spinal_no_custom_fitting_documentation:
the custom fitting documentation is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the item is a custom fitted spinal orthosis.
